# Database locking (Kanban Board API)

Follow these rules when a service reads then writes, enforces "one per logical key" (e.g. one owner, one membership row per user/board), or recalculates task/column positions.

## Stack

- **ORM:** Prisma (`$transaction`, default READ COMMITTED)
- **Helpers:** `src/common/db/` — `advisoryXactLock`, row-lock helpers, `rebalanceColumnInTx`

## When to use **pessimistic row locks** (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`)

- Read one or more rows and update/delete them in the **same transaction**
- Resource is a specific row: task delete, column delete, board member removal, single task position update where you've already resolved `prevTaskId`/`nextTaskId`

**How:** Call helpers in `src/common/db/row-lock.ts` at the start of the transaction, then read/write using the same `tx`.

## When to use **advisory locks** (`pg_advisory_xact_lock`)

Task moves are the main case here. Two users dragging tasks into the same column at the same moment can both read the same `prev`/`next` neighbors and compute the _same_ midpoint — resulting in duplicate `position` values. Serialize per-column, not per-row, since the "logical key" being contended is the column's ordering, not a single task.

- Serialize task-move position calculation within a column
- Serialize column position calculation within a board (column reorder)
- Guard column/task rebalancing so it can't run concurrently with a move in the same column
- Enforce "one `BoardMember` row per user/board" on invite (belt-and-suspenders alongside the `@@unique([boardId, userId])` constraint)

**How:**

```typescript
await advisoryXactLock(tx, `column:${columnId}:position`);
```

Use stable namespaced keys: `column:${columnId}:position`, `board:${boardId}:column-position`, `board:${boardId}:member-invite`.

## Task move pattern (fractional positioning)

```typescript
async moveTask(taskId: string, targetColumnId: string, prevTaskId?: string, nextTaskId?: string) {
  return this.prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
    // Lock the target column first — prevents concurrent moves from
    // computing the same midpoint against stale neighbor reads
    await advisoryXactLock(tx, `column:${targetColumnId}:position`);

    const task = await tx.task.findUniqueOrThrow({ where: { id: taskId } });
    const prev = prevTaskId ? await tx.task.findUnique({ where: { id: prevTaskId } }) : null;
    const next = nextTaskId ? await tx.task.findUnique({ where: { id: nextTaskId } }) : null;

    let newPosition: number;
    if (prev && next) {
      newPosition = (prev.position + next.position) / 2;
      // Gap exhausted — rebalance before writing, still inside the lock
      if (next.position - prev.position < 1e-7) {
        await rebalanceColumnInTx(tx, targetColumnId);
        return this.moveTask(taskId, targetColumnId, prevTaskId, nextTaskId); // retry with clean spacing
      }
    } else if (prev && !next) {
      newPosition = prev.position + 1;
    } else if (!prev && next) {
      newPosition = next.position / 2;
    } else {
      newPosition = 1.0;
    }

    return tx.task.update({
      where: { id: taskId },
      data: { position: newPosition, columnId: targetColumnId },
    });
  });
}
```

## Multi-step writes checklist

- [ ] All related reads/writes in one `$transaction`
- [ ] Advisory lock on the **column**, not the task, before computing a new position
- [ ] Row lock before contested delete (task/column/board-member)
- [ ] `@@unique([boardId, userId])` on `BoardMember` as final safety net for invites
- [ ] Throw `ConflictException` / `NotFoundException` — filter maps Prisma errors to 409/404
- [ ] Access-control check (board membership) happens **before** acquiring any lock, not after

## Do not

- Compute a move's new position outside a transaction — two concurrent drags will collide
- Rely on `$transaction` alone for "one membership per user/board" without the `@@unique` constraint
- Lock per-task when the contention is really per-column — you'll serialize unrelated moves unnecessarily
- Swallow `P2002` — global filter maps it to 409
